# Keeps the host's build output out of the image.
#
# This file is not an optimisation. Without it, `COPY <project>/ <project>/` overwrites the obj/
# directory that `dotnet restore` just produced inside the container with the one from the developer's
# machine - whose project.assets.json and *.nuget.g.props hold absolute Windows paths to a NuGet cache
# that does not exist in a Linux container. The restore layer above it is then worthless, and what the
# publish does next is anyone's guess.
#
# ACR Tasks also fails to export the image outright when these directories are in the context, with
# "failed to get layer sha256:...: layer does not exist" - a message that says nothing about its cause
# and reappears with a different hash on every retry.

**/bin/
**/obj/

# Source control and editor state: large, changes constantly, and busts the context cache for no
# reason. .git in particular is most of the upload.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Test and tooling output.
**/TestResults/
artifacts/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# Local configuration and anything that could carry a secret into a layer. Configuration reaches the
# container through the platform's environment variables, never through the image.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/*.env
.env

# Container definitions themselves are not build inputs.
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
